{
 "definitions": {
  "scope": "the ordinary segment (100 or more contestants, crypto and ambiguous segments removed), campaign_id count 116493, 17632 organizers",
  "family": "entry_type and custom_action template mapped by hand to eleven generic families plus bonus/question/custom_other/paid/other, the same mapping analyze.py uses on the earlier dataset. A campaign 'has' a family if any of its actions maps to it, regardless of how many actions or their worth",
  "family_pair_lift": "for each pair of families, how often they appear on the same campaign against what independence would predict. lift 1.0 is independence, above 1.0 means the two ship together more than chance, below 1.0 less. conditional_b_given_a is the share of campaigns with family a that also carry family b",
  "top_combinations": "the most common exact sets of families present on a campaign (order not counted, only presence), with outcomes for campaigns holding that exact set. email_completions_per_contestant and share_completions_per_contestant are medians across the campaigns in that combination that carry the family, not the whole row",
  "reach_vs_deep": "families split into reach (visit, follow, engage: cheap, teaches little) and deep (question, content, connect_account, download, join: costs more, asks more). reach_share is reach families present over (reach plus deep) families present, among campaigns with at least one of either",
  "lead_action_family": "the family of the action in list position 0 (the first action shown), and what campaigns leading with each family produced",
  "share_position_relative_to_email": "among campaigns offering both an email action and a share-family action, whether the share action's earliest position comes before or after the email action's earliest position, and what each action completed in each group",
  "mandatory_count_vs_optional_completion": "campaigns bucketed by how many of their actions are mandatory, against the median completion rate of their optional actions and the campaign's contestants and conversion, split by method-count band since mandatory count and total method count both drift together",
  "completions_per_contestant": "entry_count (completions, not worth-weighted) divided by valid_contestants, median across campaigns or actions as stated"
 },
